            <ArticleTitle>A Rare Cause of Testicular Pain: Thrombosis of the Pampiniform Plexus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>347-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Testicular pain is a common presentation in the emergency department. The cause includes a wide array of differentials. This report highlights a case of thrombosis of the pampiniform plexus as a rare cause of testicular pain. Doppler ultrasound should be the first line investigation. Symptomatic relief with anti-inflammatory medication should be sufficient for management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
